msgid "<0/> means if. When the if is imagined, English says “if I had”, then “I would”; Estonian puts both halves in the would form: <1/> For a real if, both usually stay in the present: <2>Kui mul on aega, lähen ma kinno.</2>"
msgstr "<0/> means if. When the if is imagined, English says “if I had”, then “I would”; Estonian puts both halves in the would form: <1/> For a real if, both usually stay in the present: <2>Kui mul on aega, lähen ma kinno.</2>"

